---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';
import { authoredWidth } from '../lib/authoredWidth';

const auditImg = '16-full-audit-2026-09-12.png';
---

<Base
  title="Projects — Sebastian Rogala"
  description="Multi-tenant Education SaaS in production, Pipeforge (Claude Code orchestration), ProfitOfExile, and open-source contributions."
>
  <TopNav current="projects" />

  <main class="frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">Projects</div>
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A product in production, a personal tool I rely on daily, a community side project, and
        recurring open-source contributions. The Pipeforge walkthrough and a knowledge-base sample
        sit underneath if you want to go deeper.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content">
      <h2>Products</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="education-saas">
          <h3 class="project-title">Education SaaS</h3>
          <p class="project-position">
            Multi-tenant platform, in production with a paying customer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Course management and lead-operations across education tenants; ready to take on
            additional customers. Stack: PHP 8.4 / Symfony 7.4 LTS / Doctrine 3 /
            PostgreSQL 16 / Redis 7 backend; Twig + Stimulus + Turbo + Tailwind front-end;
            Vitest + PHPUnit + Playwright on tests. Hexagonal modular monolith with full CQRS
            at the UseCase layer, async events via Symfony Messenger, 13 business modules.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="#how-quality-gets-enforced">enforcement details ↓</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="how-quality-gets-enforced">How quality gets enforced</h2>
      <p>
        The Education SaaS runs four independent custom enforcement layers in CI, and every PR
        has to pass all four before it can merge. Behind them sit over 11,000 automated tests
        (PHP and JS unit), green as of 2026-09-12; the Playwright end-to-end suite is excluded
        from that figure because it does not run in CI.
      </p>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(auditImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${auditImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${auditImg}`}
            alt="Audit report, twelve gates and suites green in one run: dependency check, PHPStan level 8 over 3,253 files, frontend R1-R7 plus ESLint, PHPMD, both Deptrac axes, PHP unit 6,218, JS unit 1,321, integration 2,018, functional 1,828, smoke 238, E2E 298 passed"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          One run on 2026-09-12, main @ bc44177a: twelve gates and suites, zero failures. The
          four enforcement layers described below are the PHPStan, frontend, PHPMD and Deptrac
          rows.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <strong>PHPStan 2 at level 8</strong> — plus 14 project-specific custom rules:
          entity-ID safety, tenant query safety (blocks direct <code>EntityManager</code> /
          <code>Connection</code> access outside repositories), and ADR-shape rules for the
          Action / UseCase / QueryAdapter / Port catalog. The CQRS seam is enforced at this
          layer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PHPMD</strong> — hexagonal-tuned ruleset for code smells; complements PHPStan
          on style and maintainability fronts that static analysis doesn't cover.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deptrac on two axes</strong> — layer purity (Domain → Application →
          Infrastructure, with vendor imports gated by layer) and a module dependency graph
          across 13 business modules. The module-graph baseline is shrink-only: an entry can be
          removed, never added, so a new cross-module dependency fails the build rather than
          being absorbed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Custom Twig/Tailwind lint script</strong> — 7 project rules expressing UI
          conventions that off-the-shelf linters can't: component-only
          <code>&lt;twig:Button&gt;</code> (no raw <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> in pages),
          semantic-token-only Tailwind (no literal grays), required
          <code>data-component</code> attributes, no manual <code>dark:</code> variants in
          components, ADR-tied destructive-action wrapping, and target-naming in confirmation
          modals. Managed baseline for staged migration with stale-entry detection.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each layer runs independently; the baseline pattern lets new code raise the bar without
        requiring full migration of legacy code first.
      </p>

      <h2>Personal tools</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="pipeforge">
          <h3 class="project-title">Pipeforge</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Claude Code orchestration plugin and PostgreSQL MCP backend.</p>
          <p>
            I built it because I needed to coordinate work across multiple machines and parallel
            worktrees, and it turned into where I try out context-engineering patterns before
            they land on production work. Pipeline orchestration with templated commands, agent
            dispatch, skill-based prompts, and an MCP-backed tool layer over a PostgreSQL state
            store, plus a curated knowledge base of decisions about Pipeforge itself. Not a
            product, just infrastructure I use daily.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="/projects/pipeforge">walkthrough →</a>
            <span class="sep">·</span>
            <a href="/projects/kb">knowledge base →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Side projects</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="profitofexile">
          <h3 class="project-title">ProfitOfExile</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Open-source Path of Exile lab-farming tool.</p>
          <p>
            Built solo across Go / SvelteKit / Tauri (Rust) / TimescaleDB: backend, web,
            desktop overlay. Web continuously deployed; the desktop overlay went from cold start
            to usable release in ~2 weeks (v0.1.0 on 2026-03-31 → v0.6.x on 2026-04-13), and I've
            kept developing it since. A single Go backend feeds both the web (zero-install
            SvelteKit) and the Rust/Tauri desktop with OCR and in-game overlays. One source of
            truth, two delivery surfaces. Adopted by the broader community after creator
            coverage.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://profitofexile.top" target="_blank" rel="noopener">profitofexile.top →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contributions</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Anthropic Claude Code tracker</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Reproducible finding contributed to an open issue in the official tracker.</p>
          <p>
            I isolated a compact-vs-clear instruction-override asymmetry in SessionStart hook
            behavior, with a minimal reproduction, the mechanism, and a suggested fix.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/6354#issuecomment-3849990217" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue thread →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Open-source contributions</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Recurring contributor to community tooling.</p>
          <p>
            <code>veiset/poe-vendor-string</code> (Path of Exile community tool): recurring
            contributor across map mod filtering (prefix/suffix grouping), trade-search
            integration (map yield, quality, 8-mod filter, corrupted include/exclude, instant
            buyout default), and bug fixes.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>obra/superpowers</code>: I proposed smart question batching, with a measured
            reduction in <code>AskUserQuestion</code> calls.
          </p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/SebRogala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/SebRogala →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <a href="/">← back home</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .frame {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 32px;
  }

  /* Topnav lives in src/components/TopNav.astro. */
  /* `.sep` is also used in the page footer below — keep as page-level rule. */
  .sep {
    color: var(--rule-2);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 3.03125rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .content {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 32px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.9375rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 56px 0 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .content h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .content strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .content em {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(125, 179, 108, 0.4);
  }

  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .project-list > li {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .project-list > li:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }
  .project-list > li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }
  /* When the enforcement section uses .project-list, its items are
     short bulleted entries — restore list markers and tighten spacing. */
  #how-quality-gets-enforced + p + .project-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  #how-quality-gets-enforced + p + .project-list > li {
    border-top: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .project-position {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .project-affordances {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    margin-top: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .project-affordances a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .project-affordances a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }


  .audit-figure {
    /* Capped inline at the capture's authored width. The cap lives on the
       figure, so the caption below shares exactly the image's width. */
    margin: 20px auto 28px;
  }
  .audit-figure a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .audit-figure a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .audit-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .audit-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .page-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .page-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .page-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .frame {
      padding: 36px 22px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2.1875rem;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 1.09375rem;
    }
    .content h2 {
      font-size: 1.59375rem;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .content {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    .project-title {
      font-size: 1.15625rem;
    }
  }
</style>
